  "slug": "docking-dynamics-049f",
  "summary": "Four preprints apply deep learning and computational platforms to predict Cas12a efficiency, base-editor guide choice, and A-to-I RNA editing sites.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is predicting editing outcomes from sequence context, now extending from DNA to RNA editing. 2CaP-5 predicts LbCas12a crRNA efficiency in wheat protoplasts from about 1,000 tested guides and can be retrained with 500 crRNAs. BEguided supports variant-specific guide design across 38 base-editor profiles, with BEguidedOFF for off-target prediction. Two A-to-I studies address ADAR-mediated editing: ModFormer combines sequence with predicted secondary structure to predict sites, rates and responses to mutations, while EditFinder predicts sites and variant effects from sequence alone. What is new is the inclusion of RNA structure and variant-effect prediction, plus systematic cross-editor comparison. All four are preprints, and the summaries report no head-to-head benchmarks against established tools.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
